+## Error-state UX re-verification (rotation surface, PASS)
+
+- Offline (browser-level offline emulation) send → same graceful inline `webhook-offline` bubble; no crash.
+- Back online → `[Self-Healing] Device back online. Restoring network connection state.` — automatic recovery
+  confirmed. Error-state and recovery behavior match the 2026-10-28 morning PASS (F-6-era pattern intact).
+
+## Why this addendum instead of a comment
+
+The bridge has no issue-comment tool in the anonymous toolset; the chat-dead symptom materially widens the
+#2258 fix's regression scope (chat send E2E must be included) and confirms the fix is middleware-only
+(server POST already 200). Report-only WO, zero runtime paths, file lands under docs/reports/.
+
+## Alternatives rejected
+
+- **New standalone WO for "chat broken"**: would duplicate F-12 — same middleware, same allow-list, same fix.
+- **Waiting for the fixer to rediscover chat impact**: risks a fix validated only against register, shipping
+  with chat still broken.
+- **Re-testing with modified client headers (drop the disallowed ones)**: would mask the bug and violate the
+  no-workaround-in-QA discipline; the app's headers exist for tracing/CSRF/fingerprint features.
